Addresses INV-bamij's C# half, the last of its languages. The sweep
recorded C# as a different defect, zero calls edges even inside a named
method, and that still held on dev ecab74be2e. When neither the local table
nor the resolver bound the name, the call arm emitted nothing (there was
no else branch), and a name with 3+ repository candidates hit a bare
`continue`. So every framework call vanished: File.ReadAllText,
Console.WriteLine, Marshal.PtrToStructure.

Both paths now emit make_unresolved_edge. The module slot is the
receiver's spelling only when it names a type: capitalised, not a tracked
local, and not a member of the enclosing class. PascalCase also spells
properties, and a member name in the slot is INV-kotob's defect. Otherwise
the slot is `external`, with call_construct=method when a receiver exists.
The ambiguity guard still withholds the binding, just no longer the edge.

A call in no method (a static field's lambda) is anchored on the enclosing
class/struct/interface/record/enum, else the file.

A/B on sherpa-onnx (the only C# repository on disk), dev ecab74be2e pinned
worktree vs this branch: csharp calls 213 -> 608 (+395, 0 lost; anchors:
method 335, class 39, constructor 21). Module slots: external 223, Console
45, Marshal 40, Array 19, PortAudio 14, HelpText 10, Environment 7, ...
Sampled sites read back correct (Array.Copy -> Array, Marshal.PtrToStructure
-> Marshal, callbackHandle.Free() -> external).

Not changed: object creation and method references in a field initialiser
still need an enclosing method. Pins moved: signature_axis csharp.py
445->447, 1651->1722.

